-- חוק חופשה שנתית, התשי"א-1951 — sections 1 to 8, 10, 13, 15, 33 and 38:
-- what "the leave" and a work year are, every employee's right to it, its
-- length by seniority and in proportion to the days worked, the temporary
-- wage-earner §3 does not reach, the days not counted as leave, when the
-- leave is given and the day the employee chooses, accumulation and
-- continuity, holiday pay, redemption on leaving, the payment for a
-- temporary wage-earner, that a State employee is like any other, and that
-- the law takes away no better right. The text is laws/annual-leave-law.toml,
-- pinned from the live page of ספר החוקים הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy
-- (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: the takanon's §§1.25.1-1.25.2 (the school recesses and
-- their pay), §8.1 (an instructor's days), §14.5 (an ulpan teacher's), §§1.30
-- and 2.1.8 (a substitute's vacation money) and the wage agreement of
-- 19.10.2022 (§29, two days of the teacher's choosing) rule on the subjects
-- of these sections without citing the law. Unlike the Sick Pay Law, it
-- leaves no employee under a collective agreement out, and §33 makes a State
-- employee like any other, so it reaches every teacher here.
--
-- Time is counted as the law counts it: leave in days, of which one weekly
-- rest in every seven is part (§3(א)), the work in days worked in the work
-- year, which begins on 1 January (§1). A procedure the Minister sets by
-- regulation (§3(א)'s longer leave, §7(ב)) is not pinned; no rule here turns
-- on one. The schedule (תוספת) §6(ב) names is not pinned either: the days
-- it lists are an input of the rule that reads it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties

§ `חוק חופשה שנתית — אורך החופשה, מועדה, דמי החופשה ופדיונה`

§§ `1`

-- "The leave": the annual leave owed to an employee under this law. "A
-- wage-earner": one whose pay, in whole or in part, is not paid by the month
-- or a longer period. "A work year": twelve months beginning on 1 January.
-- (A labour inspector and a leave fund are defined for sections not pinned.)
@ref law:1
GIVEN `paid, in whole or in part, other than by the month or a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a wage-earner as section 1 of the Annual Leave Law means` `paid, in whole or in part, other than by the month or a longer period` IF
    `paid, in whole or in part, other than by the month or a longer period`

@ref law:1
`the Annual Leave Law's work year begins on (MMDD)` MEANS 101

#ASSERT `a wage-earner as section 1 of the Annual Leave Law means` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a wage-earner as section 1 of the Annual Leave Law means` FALSE

§§ `2`

-- Every employee is entitled to leave, given under this law.
@ref law:2
`section 2 gives every employee leave` MEANS TRUE

§§ `3`

-- (א): the leave for each work year with one employer or at one workplace
-- is 16 days for each of the first five years, 18 for the sixth, 21 for the
-- seventh, and from the eighth a day more each year up to 28; the Minister
-- may set longer leave by regulation; one weekly rest in every seven days
-- of leave is counted in it. (ב): where the relation lasted the whole work
-- year, an employee who worked 200 days or more has those days, and fewer,
-- a share as the days worked bear to 200. (ג): where it lasted part of the
-- year, the same against 240. A part of a day of leave is not counted.
@ref law:3
GIVEN `the year of work with the employer` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for the first
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of leave section 3(א) gives for the year` `the year of work with the employer` IS
    BRANCH IF `the year of work with the employer` AT MOST 5 THEN 16
           IF `the year of work with the employer` EQUALS 6 THEN 18
           IF `the year of work with the employer` EQUALS 7 THEN 21
           OTHERWISE min 28 (21 PLUS (`the year of work with the employer` MINUS 7))

@ref law:3
`most days of leave section 3 gives a year` MEANS 28

@ref law:3
GIVEN `the year of work with the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `the relation lasted the whole work year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days he worked in the work year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of leave section 3 gives` `the year of work with the employer` `the relation lasted the whole work year` `days he worked in the work year` IS
    IF `days he worked in the work year` AT LEAST `the days that earn the whole leave`
    THEN `the whole leave`
    ELSE TRUNC (`the whole leave` TIMES `days he worked in the work year` DIVIDED BY `the days that earn the whole leave`) 0
    WHERE
        `the whole leave` MEANS `days of leave section 3(א) gives for the year` `the year of work with the employer`
        `the days that earn the whole leave` MEANS
            IF `the relation lasted the whole work year` THEN 200 ELSE 240

-- One weekly rest in every seven days of leave is counted in it: the law's
-- days are days of the calendar, and seven of them are a week of leave
-- whatever days the employee works in a week. (What an instrument's days
-- are measured against: convention instruments.leave-days-measure.)
@ref law:3
GIVEN `days of leave under the law` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks of leave the law's days make` `days of leave under the law` IS
    `days of leave under the law` DIVIDED BY 7

#ASSERT `days of leave section 3(א) gives for the year` 1 EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `days of leave section 3(א) gives for the year` 6 EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `days of leave section 3(א) gives for the year` 8 EQUALS 22
#ASSERT `days of leave section 3(א) gives for the year` 14 EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `days of leave section 3(א) gives for the year` 30 EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `days of leave section 3 gives` 3 TRUE 210 EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `days of leave section 3 gives` 3 TRUE 100 EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `days of leave section 3 gives` 3 FALSE 40 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `weeks of leave the law's days make` 28 EQUALS 4

§§ `4`

-- (א): §3 does not apply to a wage-earner who worked fewer than 75
-- consecutive days with one employer or at one workplace, in one work year
-- or two consecutive ones; he is paid for the leave as chapter 3 says
-- (§15). (ב): days are consecutive across reserve duty, the weekly rest, a
-- holiday or May Day, leave or a recess given by law or with the employer's
-- consent, a strike or lockout, an accident or illness, mourning, a
-- temporary break that does not end the relation, and emergency-service
-- training.
@ref law:4
GIVEN `a wage-earner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `consecutive days worked with the employer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3 reaches the employee` `a wage-earner` `consecutive days worked with the employer` IF
    (NOT `a wage-earner`) OR `consecutive days worked with the employer` AT LEAST 75

#ASSERT `section 3 reaches the employee` FALSE 10
#ASSERT NOT `section 3 reaches the employee` TRUE 74
#ASSERT `section 3 reaches the employee` TRUE 75

§§ `5`

-- (א): these days are not counted among the days of leave: reserve duty;
-- a holiday on which no one works, by law, agreement or custom (but not the
-- weekly rest); the birth and parenthood period; days he cannot work for an
-- accident or illness; mourning; a strike or lockout; days of notice of
-- dismissal beyond fourteen. (ב): where such days fall in the leave, the
-- leave stops for them and is made up, as far as possible, in the same work
-- year.
@desc A day section 5(א) of the Annual Leave Law does not count as a day of leave.
DECLARE `a day the Annual Leave Law does not count as leave` IS ONE OF
    `a day of reserve duty`
    `a holiday no one works, other than the weekly rest`
    `a day of the birth and parenthood period`
    `a day unable to work for an accident or illness`
    `a day of mourning`
    `a day of a strike or lockout`
    `a day of notice of dismissal beyond the fourteenth`

@ref law:5
GIVEN `days of the leave` IS A NUMBER
      `days in it section 5(א) does not count` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of leave the period gives under section 5` `days of the leave` `days in it section 5(א) does not count` IS
    max 0 (`days of the leave` MINUS `days in it section 5(א) does not count`)

-- (ב): the days the leave lost are owed again, to be made up in the year.
@ref law:5
GIVEN `days in the leave section 5(א) does not count` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days section 5(ב) makes up in the work year` `days in the leave section 5(א) does not count` IS
    `days in the leave section 5(א) does not count`

#ASSERT `days of leave the period gives under section 5` 62 10 EQUALS 52
#ASSERT `days section 5(ב) makes up in the work year` 10 EQUALS 10

§§ `6`

-- (א): the leave is given in the last month of the work year it is for,
-- or during the next one. (ב): notwithstanding, an employee may take one
-- day of the leave during the year it is for, on a date he chooses, and
-- one more on a day the schedule names (without prejudice to §5), provided
-- he told his employer at least 30 days ahead. (ג): the Minister may add to
-- the schedule by order. The day is the employee's to choose: the section
-- asks his notice, not the employer's consent.
@desc What the Annual Leave Law lets an employee do, or forbids an employer.
DECLARE `Annual Leave Law act` IS ONE OF
    `take a day of the leave on a date the employee chose`
    `take a day of the leave on a day the schedule names`
    `refuse a day of the leave the employee chose on due notice`

@ref law:6
GIVEN `the month of the work year it is for` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 to 12, or 13 and on for the next work year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6(א) lets the leave be given then` `the month of the work year it is for` IF
    `the month of the work year it is for` AT LEAST 12 AND `the month of the work year it is for` AT MOST 24

@ref law:6
`days section 6(ב) lets the employee choose in a work year` MEANS 2

@ref law:6
`days of notice section 6(ב) asks` MEANS 30

@ref law:6
`section 6(ב) asks the employer's consent` MEANS FALSE

@ref law:6
GIVEN `days of notice he gave the employer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6(ב) lets him take the day he chose` `days of notice he gave the employer` IF
    `days of notice he gave the employer` AT LEAST `days of notice section 6(ב) asks`

@ref law:6
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Annual Leave Law act`
DECIDE `the day of the employee's choosing` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `refuse a day of the leave the employee chose on due notice`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "Annual Leave Law, section 6(ב): an employee may take a day of his leave on a date he chooses, on 30 days' notice"

#ASSERT `section 6(א) lets the leave be given then` 12
#ASSERT `section 6(א) lets the leave be given then` 20
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(א) lets the leave be given then` 7
#ASSERT `section 6(ב) lets him take the day he chose` 30
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(ב) lets him take the day he chose` 29

§§ `7`

-- (א): the leave does not accumulate; but the employee, with the
-- employer's consent, may take only seven days at least and add the rest
-- to the leave of the two work years after. (ב): the Minister may forbid it
-- by regulation for health or the circumstances of the work.
@ref law:7
GIVEN `days of the year's leave` IS A NUMBER
      `the employer consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days section 7 lets him carry to the next two years` `days of the year's leave` `the employer consents` IS
    IF `the employer consents`
    THEN max 0 (`days of the year's leave` MINUS 7)
    ELSE 0

#ASSERT `days section 7 lets him carry to the next two years` 16 FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `days section 7 lets him carry to the next two years` 16 TRUE EQUALS 9

§§ `8`

-- The leave is continuous; with the employee's and the employer's consent,
-- and the workers' committee's approval where there is one, it may be
-- split, so long as one part of it is at least seven days.
@ref law:8
GIVEN `the longest part of the leave` IS A NUMBER
      `split with both sides' consent and the committee's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the leave is in one part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the leave is given as section 8 asks` `the longest part of the leave` `split with both sides' consent and the committee's approval` `the leave is in one part` IF
        `the leave is in one part`
    OR  (`split with both sides' consent and the committee's approval` AND `the longest part of the leave` AT LEAST 7)

#ASSERT `the leave is given as section 8 asks` 16 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the leave is given as section 8 asks` 5 TRUE FALSE

§§ `10`

-- (א): the employer pays for the days of leave holiday pay equal to the
-- employee's regular wage. (ב)(1): for one paid by the month or a longer
-- period, the wage he would have had for the same time had he gone on
-- working; (2) for a wage-earner, the average daily wage (the quarter
-- before the leave divided by ninety, or the fullest quarter of the twelve
-- months, as he chooses) times the days of leave. (ג): the wage is every
-- payment for the regular hours, unless a collective agreement the Minister
-- approved says otherwise; a payment for expenses the leave does not incur
-- is not wage.
@ref law:10
GIVEN `the wage he would have had working the same time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `holiday pay section 10 gives one paid by the month` `the wage he would have had working the same time` IS
    `the wage he would have had working the same time`

@ref law:10
GIVEN `the wage of the quarter he chose` IS A NUMBER
      `days of the leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `holiday pay section 10 gives a wage-earner` `the wage of the quarter he chose` `days of the leave` IS
    (`the wage of the quarter he chose` DIVIDED BY 90) TIMES `days of the leave`

#ASSERT `holiday pay section 10 gives a wage-earner` 9000 16 EQUALS 1600
#ASSERT `holiday pay section 10 gives one paid by the month` 100 EQUALS 100

§§ `13`

-- An employee who stops working before he was given the leave owed him up
-- to that day is paid its redemption, equal to the holiday pay he would
-- have had had he gone on leave that day.
@ref law:13
GIVEN `days of leave owed him on the day he stopped` IS A NUMBER
      `a day's holiday pay on that day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `redemption section 13 gives` `days of leave owed him on the day he stopped` `a day's holiday pay on that day` IS
    `days of leave owed him on the day he stopped` TIMES `a day's holiday pay on that day`

#ASSERT `redemption section 13 gives` 2 100 EQUALS 200

§§ `15`

-- (א): for a wage-earner who worked at least one day, but fewer than 75
-- consecutive days (§4), with no written contract for more than 74, the
-- employer pays a leave payment of at least 4% of the wage. (ב)-(ה): it is
-- paid to the branch's leave fund or as regulations set, returned to the
-- employer when the work goes on past 74 days (holiday pay or redemption
-- then being paid), and given to the employee as the fund's rules or the
-- regulations say.
@ref law:15
`the least share of the wage section 15 pays for the leave` MEANS 4 DIVIDED BY 100

@ref law:15
GIVEN `the wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the least leave payment section 15 requires` `the wage` IS
    `the wage` TIMES `the least share of the wage section 15 pays for the leave`

#ASSERT `the least leave payment section 15 requires` 1000 EQUALS 40

§§ `33`

-- For this law, a State employee is like any other employee.
@ref law:33
`section 33 makes a State employee like any other` MEANS TRUE

§§ `38`

-- The law takes away no right an employee has under a law, a collective
-- agreement, a contract of employment or a custom: for a right measured in
-- one number, the larger stands.
@ref law:38
GIVEN `what the law gives` IS A NUMBER, `what the agreement, contract or custom gives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what stands under section 38 of the Annual Leave Law` `what the law gives` `what the agreement, contract or custom gives` IS
    max `what the law gives` `what the agreement, contract or custom gives`

#ASSERT `what stands under section 38 of the Annual Leave Law` 28 60 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `what stands under section 38 of the Annual Leave Law` 2 0 EQUALS 2
